    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d15">

                <pb facs="0085" n="11" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg11"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/3697a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Diplomatic Representatives
                        in All Countries except Russia </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d15-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On April 6 Congress declared and President proclaimed that a state of war exists
                    between the United States and the Imperial German Government. So inform the
                    Government to which you are accredited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d15-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d15-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram to the Ambassador in Russia printed in <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_20">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1918, Russia, Vol. I, p.
                        20</ref>.</p>
